<title>UK: Food retailer Tesco to keep ban on genetically altered maize.</title>
<headline>Food retailer Tesco to keep ban on genetically altered maize.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Major U.K. supermarket chain Tesco Plc will keep its ban on the use of unprocessed genetically altered maize as an animal feed within its meat supply chain, despite a European Union decision to allow the maize to go on sale, a company spokesman said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It will implement the ban through its dedicated producer groups, called Tesco Producer Clubs, the spokesman said.</p>
<p>The European Commission earlier approved Swiss chemical giant Ciba Geigy AG's application for the market release of genetically modified maize in the EU, European farm commissioner Franz Fischler said.</p>
</text>
